{# Every flight in the booking, one direction after another: the summary line
   each direction shows on a card, then the leg-by-leg timeline underneath it.

   Both halves used to be split across a card body and its footer, which put the
   summary and the detail of the same flight in two different places.

   Each direction says whether it has been flown. Per direction and not per
   booking, because on a round trip the outbound is usually behind you while the
   return is still to come, and "this booking is in the past" cannot say that.
   A cancelled booking is not marked flown at all -- nobody was on it. #}
{% for half in halves %}
    {% if half.direction %}
        <div class="bkflights__half{{ not loop.first ? ' bkflights__half--next' : '' }}">
            <p class="booking-card__label bkflights__label">
                <span>
                    <i class="fas {{ half.icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{ half.label }}
                </span>
                {% if half.direction.flown and not booking.is_cancelled %}
                    <span class="leg-state leg-state--flown">
                        <i class="fas fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Flown
                    </span>
                {% elseif not booking.is_cancelled %}
                    <span class="leg-state leg-state--ahead">To come</span>
                {% endif %}
            </p>
            {% include 'search/cards/itinerary.html.twig' with { 'direction': half.direction } only %}
            {% include 'search/cards/itinerary-detail.html.twig' with { 'direction': half.direction } only %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
